# Python Code Quality (paste into your project's CLAUDE.md)

## Linting and Formatting

This project uses a shared pre-commit baseline from
https://github.com/m1n0/py-ai-precommit with ruff as the primary linter
and formatter.

After modifying any Python file:

```bash
ruff check --fix --show-fixes .
ruff format .
```

**Never** use `--unsafe-fixes` without explicit approval.

When ruff reports `F401` (unused import) or `F841` (unused variable), these are
intentionally marked as unfixable. Evaluate whether the import/variable is truly
unused or is an intentional re-export / placeholder before removing it.

## Pre-commit

Pre-commit hooks run on every commit. If a hook modifies files, the commit is
blocked so you can review changes. Run manually:

```bash
pre-commit run --all-files
```
